This has been a year of taking HSBC's regulatory alert contextualization pipelines from early build to real production use. I've carried end-to-end ownership of the AI/ML development on BE_L2 Recommendation, the Contextualization LOB/Legal Entity pipeline, and the Rapid2 applicability-and-categorisation engine, while also picking up the RegMap risk-taxonomy validation workstream. Below is what I delivered against each of my goals this year.
Risk & Compliance goal (mandatory)
I took direct ownership of proactively identifying and controlling risk in the models I'm accountable for, rather than waiting for issues to surface downstream.
• Productionized the BE_L2 Recommendation pipeline from a notebook into a config-driven, modular 8-stage pipeline, and found and fixed a run of production bugs myself before they became live incidents — a pyarrow schema mismatch, copy-paste key-lookup errors, and dynamic k-detection issues, among others.
• On the Contextualization LOB/Legal Entity pipeline, I traced and fixed several data-integrity risks end to end: a BigQuery upload failure on skipped rows, a NOT NULL violation on process_date_time, a silently-broken deduplication filter (confirmed it wasn't removing any already-processed alerts, fixed it, then validated the fix on a real production run — 1,002 duplicate rows correctly removed out of 1,008), and a duplicate-row bug that was double-counting certain HK-business alerts.
• Ran a rigorous out-of-time evaluation of the BE_L2 model (528 records, exact-match and cumulative accuracy breakdowns) and presented it to Srijan and Habeeb, and built a 12-test validation suite for the LOB model covering accuracy, coverage, drift, and per-component attribution.
• Kept governance documentation current under the GMRP V4.1 / GMIS framework — scoping documents, an ASDA document, and a model monitoring plan covering input drift, performance, composite score stability, and operational health — and held to the standing convention of referring to these as "solutions" rather than "models" in governance-facing materials.
Simplify and digitally transform R&C processes through AI
I was actively involved in more than the two automation activities targeted for this goal, and both are now live rather than still in pilot.
• Built and deployed BE_L2 Recommendation, which automates the scoring of compliance alerts and recommends Business Entity L2/LOB classifications using an XGBoost and Word2Vec-based composite scoring model.
• Built and deployed the Contextualization Legal Entity/LOB pipeline, the sibling recommendation stage that automates Legal Entity suggestions for the same alert population.
• On the RCM Tracker, the LOB/Legal capability I own is recorded with an expected benefit of 3 FTE — direct evidence toward the FTE-reduction target for this goal.
• Re-architected supporting controls rather than just the model itself: a monthly reference-data refresh pipeline (BE_L2_RefDataRefresh), a corrected deduplication control so alerts aren't rescored, and a monitoring plan intended to replace ad hoc manual checks with a standard MRM-aligned process.
